Z||000000||1FST2M6||05-21-2000||04:55 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header4.jpg"> <P><BR>well my headers are on.. haven't had a chance to dyno them yet... but have put over 100 miles on them and they are still as clean and shiney as when i got them back from Jet Hot (thermal protective barrier coating.. NOT ceramic.. not sure what the difference is but there is a difference). Today was Porsche Day at the shop I'll run the car on the dyno later in the week. and let ya know how it works out. the oil dip stick has to be removed for the install of these headers  and refitted around the bottom flange and in between the exhaust tubing. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-21-2000||05:01 PM||||oh also notice the nice new tranny... 4:10 from Mr.Fiero. (Thank you) The shop replaced the bearings and seals and buttoned it all up... not sure that the car is any faster but it sure pulls harder and i can ROAST the tires into 3rd instead of just a nice chirp... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-21-2000).]||||reg||1
