Z||000007||1FST2M6||05-21-2000||10:31 PM||||yeah thats my girlfriend... she and I do most of the work.. Ed guides us if we're in a bind... (no problems in clutches though we have it down to a science, not exactly a good thing though) for all the last clutch installs.. (5 of them, and one 87 4cyl, oh and BlackGTs) we start friday after work @ 6ish and leave around 8 with the motor out of the car and the tranny off... saturday morning the clutchman comes and turns the flywheel or drops off a new one (trashed 2 of them) and the car is back together by 1 and driving out the door by 3:30-4. Shes great! (Lyndsay) She put her OWN struts and springs on her Saturn, changed her intake (K&N FIPK)  thats me with my head cut off in the 3rd pic...  The headers look SWEET in the engine bay and seem to help (measured with our BOOTY-o-meter) the real numbers will come soon. as for all the rest of the work on my car.. I did the suspension mods, the weight reduction stuff (with Eds watchful eye) the nitrous I did but it was checked by Ed before i activated it, (I didn't put a fuse in to the solenoid power - thats all i did wrong) The exhaust another shop did with Ed telling them what we needed for our performance goals. And the Valve seals the shop did (Ramona yep GIRL mechanic!) and the 4:10 tranny refresh Ed did that. Lynds and I do just about everthing but have it checked out just to make sure... Its fun, Its cheaper and its a mutual interest. (oh Ed is the Owner and ASE Master Tech with M.E. degree from Ga. Tech - met him in class hes friends with the Professor)and (the back of the head in the 2nd pic is James ASE Master tech Physics Masters from UCLA I think.. some Calif univ.) hes THE Turbo MAN!||||reg||10
Z||000008||1FST2M6||05-21-2000||10:39 PM||||TR7 with Rover stock 3.8 Litre V8 (NOT 6) uum Dodge Stealth (Green) R/T TT 2 bent con rods (not so bright owner pulled vacuum lines off turbo) "for more boost" yep 26psi and BOOOOOOM!he made it about 2 days like that. and the TR Motorsport wheel you see (5 Spoke in 1st pick on right) is RX7 TT 18psi in for White Guage faces by NR, and Blitz Blow off valves. Car FAR right (solid alum wheel) '72 240 Z, with a Turbo Tom set-up and TEC-II. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||05-22-2000||12:15 AM||||I like the headers!!!!!  You have a very nice lookin shop to do all your work, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats a big help and It looks like alot of work going on in there??? I'm sure having ASE mechanics/masters, over seeing you is a big plus also.<P>Whats with the clutches?, are you running a *SPECIAL* on clutch jobs?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||05-22-2000||08:44 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> nope.. no special on clutches... Lynds and I droped in a Stock, a DF Centerforce, a RAM ("kevlar race") and replaced the disc in my 4 puck with one that was cryo treated for longer life (did that this time.. no wear on the disc that was really obvious or nasty) we turned the flywheel and hit the pressure plate with a "sctatch pad" on an angle grinder... not as uniform a surface but it works. The shop is 8100sq.ft. w/3 lifts. and 9 actual working areas with these cool car lifts... pick the car up to working height so you son't have to bend over as much... (made by Chief, the frame machine people)  the headers turned out nice BUT they would be VERY!!! hard to put on with the motor in the car the dip stick has to be disconnected from the block and the alternator has to come off... I pulled the tranny and had it back on in less than 3 hours but the head pipes and y pipe took almost 2 hours with the motor OUT OF THE CAR! very much a pain.. but worth it. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||05-22-2000||10:39 AM||||Those headers look beautiful!!<P>1st: Could you share who did them for you?? FOCOA? Chris? Local shop? <P>I ordered mines from Focoa but have not arrived (5 weeks :-( ). Have my engine/cradle out jst waiting for them.||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||05-22-2000||11:28 AM||||Chris West made them but JetHot coated them. THey were shipped out 3 days after i ordered them and  UPS screwed up our shipping so they didn't get here for 7 days.. they had a Blue label on them and everything (blue label is 3 day) they fit nice sealed up great the engine bay stays just as cool as it did with the wrapped manifolds! But including 3 day shipping from Chris to me in Atlanta it was $522...  ||||reg||1
